Working Principle

1. Exchange Connection

The program securely connects to both Binance Futures and Bitget Futures using authenticated API keys. It creates the required digital signatures for Bitget requests and establishes communication with both exchanges. 


---

2. Live Market Monitoring

Every three seconds the bot fetches the latest futures price of the selected cryptocurrency from both exchanges.

It continuously compares:

Binance Futures Price

Bitget Futures Price


This allows the system to identify temporary price differences between exchanges. 


---

3. Arbitrage Opportunity Detection

The software calculates the percentage difference (Gap) using:

Gap (%) = ((Bitget Price − Binance Price) ÷ Binance Price) × 100

If the calculated gap exceeds the predefined threshold (0.3%), the bot considers it a profitable arbitrage opportunity. 


---

4. Automated Trade Execution

The bot automatically performs opposite trades on both exchanges.

If Bitget price is higher:

Buy (Long) on Binance Futures

Sell (Short) on Bitget Futures


If Binance price is higher:

Sell (Short) on Binance Futures

Buy (Long) on Bitget Futures


This strategy attempts to capture the price difference while reducing exposure to the overall market direction. 


---

5. Position Management

The system constantly monitors all active positions.

When prices converge or the gap reverses beyond the configured threshold, it automatically closes both positions to complete the arbitrage cycle and prepare for the next opportunity. 


---

6. Risk Management

Several safety mechanisms are implemented:

Checks available USDT balance before trading

Uses a fixed trade amount

Prevents duplicate positions

Automatically closes partially executed trades if one side fails

Validates API connectivity before operation

Uses retry mechanisms for network failures


These features improve system reliability and reduce operational risk. 


---

7. Telegram Notification System

The project integrates a Telegram Bot that sends real-time notifications whenever:

A price gap is detected

A trade is executed

A trade fails

Positions are closed

Errors occur


This allows the user to monitor the trading system remotely without constantly checking the exchanges. 


