Conclusion

This project demonstrates the practical application of Python programming, financial market analysis, API integration, automation, and software engineering. By continuously monitoring two cryptocurrency futures exchanges and automatically executing arbitrage trades, the system showcases how technology can identify and act on short-lived market inefficiencies with minimal manual intervention. It serves as an educational example of automated algorithmic trading and highlights concepts such as real-time data processing, secure API communication, risk management, and event-driven programming. 
